00:38:20.000 --> 00:39:00.000
intelligence can be improved. It's one of the reasons people love the concept of emotional intelligence is because, unlike IQ, which is kind of difficult to change very much after you're a teenager, you can improve your emotional intelligence over the course of your lifetime. Merely aging and gaining life experience typically improves your emotional intelligence. Kind of amazing that way. Now, the difference in terms of how we would go about improving our intelligence, our emotional intelligence, concerns whether we're talking about kids or adults,
智力是可以提高的。人们热爱“情商”这个概念的原因之一，是因为与智商（在青少年之后很难有太大改变）不同，情商可以在你的一生中不断提升。随着年龄的增长和生活经验的积累，你的情商通常也会随之提高。从这个角度来看，这真是相当神奇。现在，关于我们如何去提升智力与情商，其区别在于我们讨论的是孩子还是成人，

63
00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:52.000
for kids teaching these skills directly in the classroom as part of a social, emotional learning program is probably a pretty effective and efficient way to learn these skills. It's a little more difficult as adults to take a class in emotional intelligence. And so we have to look for other ways to do it. I believe, I don't have a lot of data on which to base this, but I believe that's where the arts can really help us. So imagine that when we're reading great literature and trying to understand the motives of characters and why someone is behaving as they are, why they might behave in ways that look conflicted, all of that helps us develop a more sophisticated understanding of emotions,
对于孩子们来说，在课堂上作为社交情感学习项目的一部分直接教授这些技能，可能是一种相当有效且高效的学习方式。而对于成年人来说，去上情商课则要困难一些。因此，我们必须寻找其他方法来实现这一点。我相信（虽然我没有太多的数据来支持这一点），艺术在这一方面能真正地帮到我们。想象一下，当我们阅读伟大的文学作品，试图理解角色的动机、他们为什么会有某种行为、为什么他们的行为可能会显得充满矛盾时，所有这些都有助于我们对情感形成更深刻的理解，

64
00:39:52.000 --> 00:40:21.000
a greater ability to recognize emotions and label them and maybe even manage them. I think having experiences where you're looking at visual art, looking at, let's say, at paintings in an art museum and reacting to them emotionally might help. In Santander, Spain, there is an entire museum, organized, art museum, organized around the idea of emotions and creativity,
从而具备更强的识别、命名甚至管理情感的能力。我认为，当你欣赏视觉艺术、比如说在艺术博物馆里看画作并在情感上做出反应时，这样的体验可能会有所帮助。在西班牙的桑坦德，有一座完整的博物馆，这是一个围绕着情感与创造力的理念来组织的艺术博物馆，

65
